      answer: 'While magnetic sliders rely on opposing NdFeB magnetic fields for smooth attraction/repulsion, mechanical EDC fidgets (27+ molds in our catalog) use 304 stainless steel compression springs, hardened ratchet pawls, bolt-action breeches, and ceramic detent balls to produce crisp, directional, watch-bezel or rifle-bolt mechanical lockup.'
    },
    {
      question: 'What are the 4 main kinematic mechanisms in the Mechanical EDC Fidgets collection?',
      answer: 'Our mechanical lineup spans (1) Linear & Rotary Spring-Ball Detent Sliders (FS-085, FS-092, FS-117, FS-127, FS-130), (2) Bolt-Action & Breech-Lock Recoil Sliders (FS-067, FS-098), (3) Planetary Gear & Articulated Track Chains (FS-068, FS-087, FS-146), and (4) Centrifugal Flick & Chaotic Pendulum Linkages (FS-089, FS-090).'
    },
    {
      question: 'Why do you use Zirconia (ZrO2) and Silicon Nitride (Si3N4) ceramic detent balls instead of carbon steel balls?',
      answer: 'Plain carbon steel balls pressed under continuous spring preload against a metal track cause adhesive micro-welding (galling) within 5,000 cycles. Upgrading to Vickers 1,400–1,600 HV ceramic detent beads or pairing hardened steel balls with self-lubricating virgin PTFE blocks (FS-127) reduces friction below μ = 0.08 and guarantees 100,000+ wear-free clicks.'
    },
    {
      question: 'Can end-users customize the spring count and click resistance on models like FS-117 and FS-085?',
      answer: 'Yes! Models like FS-117 (Arachnid 8-Spring Mechanical Slider) and FS-085 (CNC Aluminum Dual-Spring Ratchet EDC) feature removable precision Torx/hex covers so users can populate 2, 4, 6, or all 8 spring-and-bead chambers to tune actuation force and acoustic loudness.'
    },
    {
      question: 'Do mechanical EDC fidgets come with spare springs and ceramic detent beads?',
      answer: 'Yes. Every serviceable spring-detent mechanical SKU shipped from our factory automatically includes a heat-sealed spare maintenance pack containing extra SUS304 stainless springs and replacement detent beads inside the box.'
    },
    {
      question: 'Which mechanical EDC models are quietest for executive office use vs. loudest for tactile enthusiasts?',
      answer: 'For quiet office use (45–56 dBA), choose PTFE-buffered spring sliders (FS-127), anodized aluminum bamboo ratchets (FS-092), or continuous planetary gear tracks (FS-068). For authoritative metallic clicks (66–74 dBA), choose the Bolt-Action Spring Breech Slider (FS-067) or Arachnid 8-Spring Slider (FS-117).'
    },
    {
      question: 'How do you prevent compression springs from losing tension ("spring set") over time?',
      answer: 'We wind all detent springs from cold-drawn SUS304 stainless steel or SWP-B music wire (Ø0.35mm–Ø0.50mm wire diameter) and perform factory shot-peening and thermal stress-relief stabilization so spring rate (1.8–3.4 N/mm) never degrades.'
    },
    {
      question: 'Are pure mechanical ratchet fidgets (FS-067, FS-068, FS-085, FS-092, FS-117) 100% magnet-free?',
      answer: 'Yes. Pure spring-and-gear mechanical models contain zero rare-earth magnets, making them ideal for customers who work around sensitive magnetic instruments, mechanical watches, or air-freight routes without IATA PI-953 magnetic shielding.'
    },
    {
      question: 'Where can custom brand logos be engraved on multi-part mechanical fidgets?',
      answer: 'We fiber-laser engrave logos onto the flat side receiver plates, spine rails, pocket clips, or center bearing caps (such as on FS-067, FS-085, FS-087, and FS-127) with a 100-piece MOQ and $0 mold fee.'
    },
    {
      question: 'Can we order a mixed sample kit of bolt-action, ratchet, and planetary gear EDC fidgets?',
      answer: 'Yes. Contact our engineering desk via /contact to order a curated Mechanical EDC Sample Pack before locking in your 50-piece blank or 100-piece custom logo bulk production.'
    }
  ],
  'haptic-fidget-coins-edc-gourds-magnetic-spinner-rings-guide': [
    {
      question: 'Why should wholesale EDC buyers stock Haptic Coins, Gourds, and Spinner Rings alongside rectangular sliders?',
      answer: 'One-handed ergonomics vary by customer preference: circular Haptic Coins offer continuous 360-degree rotary indexing without resetting thumb position, EDC Gourds & Capsules provide organic palm-rolling wellness relief, and Magnetic Spinner Rings offer zero-pocket-bulk wearable fidgeting.'
    },
    {
      question: 'How do 12-magnet rotary Haptic Fidget Coins (FS-013, FS-030, FS-053) work?',
      answer: 'Two circular metal shells (Ø38mm–Ø45mm) rotate around a central pivot screw or R188 bearing while housing concentric rings of 12 N52/N54 neodymium magnets spaced at 30° intervals. Twisting the top shell 15° overcomes magnetic shear and snaps it into the next pole alignment.'
    },
    {
      question: 'What is the difference between magnetic haptic coins and ceramic-bead ratchet coins (FS-032, FS-041, FS-071)?',
      answer: 'Magnetic coins (FS-013, FS-030, FS-033, FS-053) provide frictionless magnetic repulsion-attraction snaps and can also be clicked open like a clamshell. Ceramic-bead ratchet coins (FS-032, FS-041, FS-071) use spring-loaded zirconia beads riding on a CNC wave ring for a crisp safe-dial mechanical click.'
    },
    {
      question: 'What are modern CNC EDC Gourds (Hu-Lu) and Palm Capsules (FS-012, FS-096, FS-099, FS-105, FS-107)?',
      answer: 'Inspired by traditional East Asian Baoding palm pieces, our 5-axis CNC gourds and capsules divide a contoured barrel into independently rotating magnetic waist chambers, R188 spinning bases, and internal acoustic chime bells—coupled with a lanyard bail for keychain or bag carry.'
    },
    {
      question: 'Why is FS-099 machined from translucent Amber PEI (Ultem) polymer?',
      answer: 'Aerospace polyetherimide (PEI / Ultem 1000) weighs only 46g (37% lighter than aluminum), stays naturally warm to the touch in winter, resists chemical/sweat corrosion, and showcases the internal magnetic and bearing assembly through its golden-amber body.'
    },
    {
      question: 'How are wearable Magnetic Spinner Rings (FS-014, FS-069, FS-119, FS-135, FS-140) engineered for finger comfort?',
      answer: 'Our spinner rings feature a stationary inner band CNC-bored from hypoallergenic 304/316 surgical stainless steel or anodized aluminum with an R1.5mm parabolic comfort-fit interior chamfer (Ø18mm–Ø22mm ID) so the outer band spins effortlessly without pinching skin.'
    },
    {
      question: 'What is the difference between 16-magnet spinner rings (FS-135, FS-140) and 8-bead spring rings (FS-119)?',
      answer: '16-magnet spinner rings (FS-135, FS-140) pack 16 micro neodymium magnets into the rotating band (22.5° per pulse) for whisper-quiet, zero-wear tactile feedback. The 8-bead ring (FS-119) uses spring-loaded detent beads for a louder, mechanical gear-click sensation.'
    },
    {
      question: 'How do you engrave custom logos onto curved Gourds, Coins, and inside Ring bores?',
      answer: 'For Haptic Coins, we laser engrave the flat center medallion cap or perimeter rim. For cylindrical Gourds and Eggs, we use a 360° synchronized CNC rotary chuck. For Spinner Rings, we use a micro-galvo jewelry laser to engrave your brand mark inside the inner stainless steel bore.'
    },
    {
      question: 'Do Haptic Coins, Gourds, and Spinner Rings comply with US CPSC 16 CFR 1262 magnet safety rules?',
      answer: 'Yes. All internal magnets in our coins, gourds, and rings are permanently sealed inside CNC-counterbored pockets beneath threadlocked mechanical retainers and structural epoxy, passing 16 CFR 1262 drop, torque, and tension abuse tests.'
    },
    {
      question: 'What is the MOQ to launch a 3-SKU bundle of a Coin, a Gourd, and a Spinner Ring?',
      answer: 'Blank wholesale MOQ is 50 pcs per SKU, and custom logo MOQ is 100 pcs per SKU with $0 tooling fees. We can also cut custom multi-cavity EVA foam trays to present a 2-piece or 3-piece collector gift set inside a single rigid box.'
    }
  ],
  'custom-eva-zipper-cases-tin-boxes-metal-fidget-packaging-guide': [
    {
      question: 'Why do heavy metal fidgets (60g–160g) require EVA foam inserts instead of standard paperboard tuck boxes?',
      answer: 'During a 1.0-meter parcel drop, a 115g metal slider generates over 45 Gs of impact force, tearing through unpadded paperboard flaps and scratching anodized or PVD finishes. High-density closed-cell EVA foam cavities absorb kinetic shock and lock the hardware in place.'
    },
    {
      question: 'What are the 4 standard wholesale packaging tiers available at FidgetSupply.com?',
      answer: 'We offer: Tier 1 Standard Acrylic/PP Snap Case ($0.00 included in base FOB price), Tier 2 Hard-Shell 75-Shore-C EVA Zipper Carry Case (+$0.65–$1.10/pc, 100 pcs MOQ), Tier 3 Matte Windowed or Solid Tin Presentation Box with EVA foam (+$0.85–$1.45/pc, 100 pcs MOQ), and Tier 4 Rigid 1200gsm Magnetic-Flip Collector Gift Box (+$1.60–$2.80/pc, 300 pcs MOQ).'
    },
    {
      question: 'Why do you use 45–60 kg/m³ closed-cell EVA foam instead of soft open-cell polyurethane sponge?',
      answer: 'Open-cell PU sponge compresses flat under the weight of a 120g stainless steel slider during transit. Our 45–60 kg/m³ closed-cell EVA foam with black velveteen flocking maintains 98%+ dimensional recovery and is sulfur-free so it never tarnishes raw brass or copper.'
    },
    {
      question: 'Can the custom die-cut EVA foam insert hold spare PTFE stickers, springs, and authenticity cards?',
      answer: 'Yes. Every custom EVA tray we cut includes a finger-pull notch plus dedicated under-tray or side slots for spare Teflon (PTFE) friction pads, replacement springs/ceramic beads, microfiber cloths, and serialized collector cards.'
    },
    {
      question: 'Do you apply Amazon FNSKU barcodes and 14+ CPSC safety warning labels at the factory?',
      answer: 'Yes. On all orders of 100+ units, our packing line prints and applies smudge-proof thermal Amazon FNSKU/UPC barcodes, country-of-origin markings, and US CPSC 16 CFR 1262 / EU CE 14+ age-grading warning labels at $0 extra labor cost.'
    },
    {
      question: 'How does your packaging pass IATA PI-953 magnetic air-freight inspections for DHL and FedEx?',
      answer: 'To keep external stray magnetic fields below 0.00525 Gauss at 2.1 meters per IATA PI-953, we combine ferromagnetic 0.23mm tinplate boxes (which shunt 65% of dipole flux), alternating North-South checkerboard carton packing, and 0.35mm silicon-iron shielding sheets lining the master carton walls.'
    },
    {
      question: 'What are your master export carton specifications for Amazon FBA inbound compliance?',
      answer: 'We pack 100 units per 5-ply BC-flute double-wall master carton (45 × 35 × 30 cm, 44 ECT crush rating) lined with 10mm EPE pearl cotton, keeping gross carton weight between 11.5 kg and 14.8 kg—strictly below Amazon FBA’s 15.0 kg / 50 lb safety cap.'
    },
    {
      question: 'Can we combine 2 or 3 different fidget SKUs under a single 100-piece custom-branded EVA case or tin box order?',
      answer: 'Yes! Because the outer EVA zipper case or tin box lid carries your brand logo and the interior EVA foam cavities are cut in-house, you can split a 100-piece packaging run across 2 different fidget models (50 pcs + 50 pcs).'
    },
    {
      question: 'How fast can we get a digital mockup of our logo on both the fidget hardware and the outer packaging?',
      answer: 'Submit your vector logo (.AI, .EPS, .PDF, or .SVG) via /contact and our CAD packaging desk will deliver a dual 3D proof showing both on-product laser/UV placement and outer EVA case/tin box artwork within 12 to 24 hours.'
    },
    {
      question: 'Can we order physical packaging samples along with our metal fidget evaluation samples?',
      answer: 'Yes. Request our Packaging & Hardware Evaluation Kit on /contact to inspect our Acrylic Snap Case, Hard-Shell EVA Zipper Case, Matte Tin Box, and Rigid Collector Box in person.'
    }
  ]
};

const guideFaqs = GUIDE_FAQS_BY_SLUG[guide.data.slug] || GUIDE_FAQS_BY_SLUG['zero-tooling-ready-mold-private-label-fidget-sop'];
const localizedGuideFaqs = localizeInsightFaqs(guide.data.slug, guideFaqs, currentLang);

// Dynamic Reading Time Calculation based on actual text, technical tables, and FAQ elements
const rawText = guide.body ? guide.body.replace(/<[^>]*>?/gm, ' ') : '';
const wordCount = rawText.split(/\s+/).filter((word) => word.length > 0).length;
const tableCount = (guide.body ? guide.body.match(/<table/g) || [] : []).length;
const faqCount = localizedGuideFaqs.length;
const computedReadingMinutes = Math.max(
  8,
  Math.round(wordCount / 160 + tableCount * 1.5 + faqCount * 0.45)
);
const dynamicReadTime = `${computedReadingMinutes} ${t('unit.minRead')}`;

const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': ['TechArticle', 'BlogPosting'],
  headline: locGuideMeta.title,
  description: locGuideMeta.summary,
  image: [`https://fidgetsupply.com${guide.data.featuredImage}`],
  datePublished: guide.data.publishDate,
  dateModified: guide.data.updatedDate || guide.data.publishDate,
  author: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: locGuideMeta.author,
    '@id': 'https://fidgetsupply.com/#organization'
  },
  publisher: {
    '@id': 'https://fidgetsupply.com/#organization'
  }
};

const breadcrumbSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    {
      '@type': 'ListItem',
      position: 1,
      name: t('breadcrumb.home'),
      item: 'https://fidgetsupply.com'
    },
    {
      '@type': 'ListItem',
      position: 2,
      name: t('breadcrumb.guides'),
      item: 'https://fidgetsupply.com/insights'
    },
    {
      '@type': 'ListItem',
      position: 3,
      name: locGuideMeta.title,
      item: `https://fidgetsupply.com/insights/${guide.data.slug}`
    }
  ]
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: localizedGuideFaqs.map((f) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.question,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.answer }
  }))
};
---

<Layout
  title={currentLang === 'en' ? guide.data.metaTitle : `${locGuideMeta.title} | FidgetSupply`}
  description={currentLang === 'en' ? guide.data.metaDescription : locGuideMeta.summary}
  ogImage={guide.data.featuredImage}
  activePage="insights"
  jsonLd={[articleSchema, breadcrumbSchema, faqSchema]}
>
  <article class="guide-article">
    <header class="guide-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href={getLocalizedPath('/', currentLang)}>{t('breadcrumb.home')}</a> / <a href={getLocalizedPath('/insights', currentLang)}>{t('breadcrumb.guides')}</a> / <span>{locGuideMeta.category}</span>
        </nav>
        <span class="badge badge-dark">{locGuideMeta.category} · {dynamicReadTime}</span>
        <h1>{locGuideMeta.title}</h1>
        <p class="guide-lead">{locGuideMeta.summary}</p>
        <div class="guide-byline">
          <span>{t('guide.by')} <strong>{locGuideMeta.author}</strong></span>
          <span>·</span>
          <span>{t('guide.updated')} {guide.data.updatedDate || guide.data.publishDate}</span>
          <span>·</span>
          <span>{dynamicReadTime}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- 3-COLUMN BACKLINKO PUBLICATION ARCHITECTURE -->
    <div class="container article-layout-grid">
      <!-- LEFT SIDEBAR: Sticky Table of Contents -->
      <aside class="article-sidebar left-sidebar" aria-label="Table of Contents">
        <div class="sticky-wrapper">
          <h4 class="sidebar-title">{t('guide.tocTitle')}</h4>
          <nav id="toc-container" class="toc-nav">
            <!-- Dynamically populated by inline script -->
          </nav>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <!-- CENTER COLUMN: Main Skyscraper Article -->
      <div class="article-main">
        <!-- Featured Hero Image -->
        <div class="article-featured-image-wrap">
          <img
            src={guide.data.featuredImage}
            alt={guide.data.title}
            width="800"
            height="600"
            loading="eager"
          />
        </div>

        <!-- Executive Engineering Summary Callout -->
        <GeoDirectAnswer
          title={t('guide.execBriefTitle')}
          answer={locGuideMeta.summary}
        />

        <!-- Main Editorial Content -->
        <div class="prose article-body clean-editorial-content" set:html={localizedGuideHtml} />

        <!-- Referenced Ready-to-Produce Factory Models -->
        {relatedProducts.length > 0 && (
          <section class="related-skus-section" id="referenced-factory-models">
            <h2>{t('guide.refModelsTitle')}</h2>
            <div class="grid-3">
              {relatedProducts.slice(0, 3).map((p: any) => (
                <ProductCard product={p} />
              ))}
            </div>
          </section>
        )}

        <!-- Related Engineering Insights Box -->
        {relatedGuides.length > 0 && (
          <section class="related-guides-box" id="related-engineering-insights">
            <span class="badge">{t('guide.continueBadge')}</span>
            <h2>{t('guide.relatedGuidesTitle')}</h2>
            <div class="related-guides-grid">
              {relatedGuides.map((rg: any) => {
                const rgLoc = localizeInsightMeta(rg.data, currentLang);
                return (
                  <a href={getLocalizedPath(`/insights/${rg.data.slug}`, currentLang)} class="related-guide-card">
                    <img src={rg.data.featuredImage} alt={rgLoc.title} width="400" height="300" loading="lazy" />
                    <div class="related-guide-body">
                      <span class="related-guide-cat">{rgLoc.category}</span>
                      <h3>{rgLoc.title}</h3>
                      <span class="related-guide-cta">{t('guides.readCta')}</span>
                    </div>
                  </a>
                );
              })}
            </div>
          </section>
        )}

        <!-- Guide 10-FAQ Section -->
        <section class="section section-light guide-faq-section" id="frequently-asked-questions">
          <div class="section-header-center">
            <span class="badge">{t('guides.faqBadge')}</span>
            <h2 class="section-title">{t('pdp.faqTitle')} — {locGuideMeta.category}</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-list">
            {localizedGuideFaqs.map((faq, idx) => (
              <div class:list={['accordion-item', { active: idx === 0 }]}>
                <button type="button" class="accordion-header">
                  <span>{faq.question}</span>
                  <span class="accordion-icon">+</span>
                </button>
                <div class="accordion-content">
                  <p>{faq.answer}</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Author & Engineering Lab Credentials Card -->
        <div class="author-credential-card">
          <div class="author-info-wrap">
            <span class="author-sub">{t('guide.authorSub')}</span>
            <h4 class="author-name">{t('guide.authorName')}</h4>
            <p class="author-bio">
              {t('guide.authorBio')}
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- RIGHT SIDEBAR: Sticky Quick Action Dock -->
      <aside class="article-sidebar right-sidebar" aria-label="Quick Sourcing Actions">
        <div class="sticky-wrapper">
          <div class="quick-rfq-dock">
            <span class="dock-badge">{t('guide.dockBadge')}</span>
            <h4>{t('guide.dockTitle')}</h4>
            <p>{t('guide.dockDesc')}</p>
            <a href={getLocalizedPath('/contact', currentLang)} class="btn btn-primary dock-cta-btn">
              {t('nav.requestQuote')}
            </a>
            <a href={getLocalizedPath('/products', currentLang)} class="btn btn-outline dock-catalog-btn">
              {t('nav.allCatalog')}
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    var tocNav = document.getElementById('toc-container');
    var articleBody = document.querySelector('.article-main');
    if (!tocNav || !articleBody) return;
    var headings = articleBody.querySelectorAll('h2');
    if (!headings.length) return;
    var ul = document.createElement('ul');
    headings.forEach(function (h, idx) {
      if (!h.id) {
        h.id = 'section-' + (idx + 1);
      }
      var li = document.createElement('li');
      var a = document.createElement('a');
      a.href = '#' + h.id;
      a.textContent = h.textContent;
      li.appendChild(a);
      ul.appendChild(li);
    });
    tocNav.appendChild(ul);
  })();
</script>

